  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Differentiate $2{x}^{2}cos\u2061(x).$\n\n$(2{x}^{2}cos\u2061(x))^{\u2032}=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,2{x}^{2}sin\u2061(x)$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=2{x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=cos\u2061(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}^{2}cos\u2061(x))^{\u2032} & ={u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})^{\u2032}\\cdot cos\u2061(x)+2{x}^{2}\\cdot (cos\u2061(x))^{\u2032} \\\\  & =(4x)(cos\u2061(x))+(2{x}^{2})(-sin\u2061(x)) \\\\  & =4xcos\u2061(x)-2{x}^{2}sin\u2061(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
